I've fixed the header issue in the Settings menu by adding `headerShown: true` to the `Stack.Screen` options. The key change was:

**Before:**
```tsx
<Stack.Screen
  options={{
    headerTitle: () => (
      // ... header content
    ),
    // ... other options
  }}
/>
```

**After:**
```tsx
<Stack.Screen
  options={{
    headerShown: true,  // ← Added this line
    headerTitle: () => (
      // ... header content
    ),
    // ... other options
  }}
/>
```

The issue was that the tab layout has `headerShown: false` in its screen options, which was overriding the header configuration in the profile screen. By explicitly setting `headerShown: true` in the profile screen's Stack.Screen options, the header will now appear with the FriendLend icon and title, matching the style of the main dashboard screen.

